<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δορῠφορ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>attend as a body-guard,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.168
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				3.127
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.130
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἔπαρχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PAmh.</u>
					2.79.52
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>: generally, <i>keep guard over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἑκάστου σωτηρίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					23.123
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴν λογισμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1.5b
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be guarded,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατοπέδοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					17.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δορυφορεῖσθαι τῇ τῶν πολιτῶν εὐνοίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					10.37
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ μανίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					573a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.239
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> Astrol.,
			of planets, <i>attend,</i> i. e. <i>flank,</i> the Sun, etc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				114
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				5.38
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat.,
				<i>attend as guard,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν αὐτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.5.84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθαρχοῦντας αὐτῷ καὶ -φοροῦντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					32.8.6
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph. of
			numbers in a series, <i>flank,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.77
			</span></i> P.:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				p.40P.
			</span></i></div>
